node_modules/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
.next/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

# workflow-agent scratch snapshots — never commit
*_models.json
modelsdev.json

# regenerable graphify artifacts (rebuilt by post-commit hook)
graphify-out/

# MemPalace per-project files (issue #185)
mempalace.yaml
entities.json

# derived: the SQLite projection is rebuildable from the trajectory (V0-02)
.harness/state.db

# A user's trajectory is THEIR data and is private by default. Joe Brown, 21 August 2026:
# "Obviously we shouldn't be shipping anyones personal logs to the public repo ... my usage of
# consilient should remain private just like anyone elses unless they agree to share data in
# which case that is private and used to improve consilient only."
# Two days of trajectory were tracked and published before this line existed. The project's own
# provenance (which ADRs were accepted, what the gates measured) is a DIFFERENT artefact and may
# be published deliberately; it must never be published as a side effect of a user's log living
# in a tracked path. Enforced by test_no_user_trajectory_is_tracked.
.harness/log/
# Immutable retained payloads are private instance data linked from the trajectory.
.harness/objects/
# Redacted share bundles are still the user's data. They are held privately if the
# user consents (ADR-0057); they must never become publishable by occupying a tracked
# path. The exporter does not exist yet. The ignore rule does, so the third leak is
# not how we discover the gap. docs/20-design/trajectory-sharing-consent-2026-08-21.md.
.harness/share/
.harness/state.db-wal
.harness/state.db-shm
# `replay` sets aside a stale projection before rebuilding; it is a local artefact,
# reproducible from the log, and not part of the record.
.harness/state.db.stale-*

# derived: the observability surface is a rendering of the trajectory (ADR-0053).
# It embeds the record's contents verbatim, so committing it would duplicate the log
# into an unreviewed artefact and hand the secret scanner a second copy to miss.
.harness/dashboard.html

# Transient runner state: a pid and a run id, meaningful only while a run is live.
# Committing it would assert a lock that is not held.
docs/10-research/experiments/*/run.lock

# EXP-27 collector runtime state: rebuilt by running the collector; not evidence.
docs/10-research/experiments/exp27/collector-state.json

# Agent transcripts. These are multi-megabyte verbatim records of dispatched runs: they carry
# whatever an agent read, printed or was told, and they sit inside the repository. Nothing in
# them belongs in the record, and a single `git add -A` would commit all of them — which is not
# hypothetical, because `git add -A` swept four brief files into a commit on 20 August 2026.
.harness/dispatch/
# EXP-50 smoke batches and other local RSI artefacts. The producing scripts are tracked;
# the generated candidates are instance data.
.harness/rsi/
# Operator quota snapshot. Local to this machine; not evidence and not publishable.
.harness/headroom.json
# Briefs written for a dispatched agent, which live in a clone's root by convention.
brief-*.md

# Raw private-corpus extracts. EXP-01 mines ../hireable-3.0 and ../jobboard-v2, whose NAMES and
# AGGREGATE METRICS may be recorded (AGENTS.md) but whose PR titles, commit messages and file
# paths may never be. The derived data files are referenced by findings documents and must not
# become committable if anyone regenerates them.
data/
*-prs.json
red-cells-evidence.json

# Pseudonym maps back to private-corpus identifiers. Local only, never published.
*.local.json

# INSTANCE spend limits and captured provider payloads. The PRODUCT ships the shape in
# .harness/limits.example.json; what a particular person is willing to spend, and any
# payload observed from their account, is theirs and stays out of a public repository.
.harness/limits.json
.harness/usage/
# INSTANCE permission mode for dispatched harnesses. PRODUCT default is bypass.
.harness/permissions.json
.harness/status.html
# INSTANCE cwd allowlist. PRODUCT ships the empty example; machine paths stay here.
# Listing a root is supervised dispatch (ADR-0063), not a Gate B pass.
.harness/allowed-cwds.json
# Exclusive lock around cursor-agent. Two processes race ~/.cursor/cli-config.json.
.harness/cursor-agent.lock
# INSTANCE private harvest (ADR-0057). Never published.
.harness/training/
# Computer-use screenshots and session dirs. Playwright is instance.
.harness/computer-use/
# INSTANCE knowledge materialisation and operator briefs. PRODUCT is the scripts.
.harness/knowledge/
.harness/briefs/
# Local EXP-96 corpus clones and lock files. The runner is tracked; the pin is not.
.harness/exp96-candidate-*/
docs/10-research/experiments/*/results-*.json.lock
# INSTANCE audit scratch output. MEASURED 26 Aug 2026: a mislabelled commit tracked 338
# duplicate files here (repeated docs/ADR copies), inflating the foreign-identifier count
# past its ceiling and tripping the tracked-file spend scanner on quoted example API names.
.harness/al-audit-scratch/
# INSTANCE timestamped plan-state backups.
.harness/plan-backups/
# INSTANCE one-shot scratch script (its own docstring: "Not product code"). MEASURED
# 26 Aug 2026: untracked once already by a4f446e with no gitignore entry, so a later
# broad `git add` re-tracked it. The entry is what a4f446e was missing.
.harness/classify_verify_out.py

# Unit worktrees are git worktrees, not content. An agent ran a bulk `git add` on
# 24 August 2026 and staged 65,923 files from under here; committing that would have
# put every nested worktree into the repository. They are working directories with
# their own git state and they are never repository content.
.harness/unit-worktrees/

# Working documents that quote the private corpora. Untracked 24 Aug 2026 after
# check_private_corpus.py found a content fingerprint in one of them; they are instance
# data and must never be tracked. See .harness/STOP-PUBLISH.
.harness/quarantine-*.md

# Mutable harness state. MEASURED 24-25 August 2026: these are written continuously by the
# driver, so tracking them made the main tree permanently dirty and the driver deferred every
# merge with "N path(s) dirty in the main tree". Tracking them is also how .harness/plan-units.json
# once silently lost a queued unit -- a git checkout restored an older copy of the file that
# decides what gets dispatched. .harness/log/ was already ignored and never suffered either.
# The files stay on disk; only the index stops carrying them. See unit Z04.
.harness/driver-state.json
.harness/plan-units.json
.harness/driver-tick.lock
.harness/*.lock
.harness/build-loop.out
.harness/build-loop.err
.harness/build-loop.*
.harness/board-snapshot.json
# Generated board: a rendering of a snapshot, same class as dashboard.html.
.harness/build-board.html
# Experiment scratch and local runner results. Instance data; a checkout
# must not restore them. .harness/exp79-scratch/log/ was a tracked JSONL
# log — the ADR-0057 leak class, one directory over from .harness/log/.
.harness/exp79-scratch/
.harness/exp130-out.txt
.harness/exp130-scratch/
.harness/fallback-result.json
.harness/stray-debris-*/
# Mutable gate-unit dump; same class as plan-units.json.
.harness/gate-specs.json

# Teardown/research clones kept under .harness. These are other people's repositories, cloned
# locally to read; committing one as a GITLINK publishes a submodule pointer to a repo this
# project does not control, and the publication gate cannot read it as a file so it fails
# closed -- which is what refused the push on 25 Aug 2026. Instance data; never tracked.
.harness/*-teardown-source-*/
.harness/*-teardown-source-*

# Orchestration and experiment scratch directories. These are per-run working copies -- two of
# them are COMPLETE extra copies of src/consilient/, so `git ls-files` returned three
# consilient/events.py and the guard-mutation registry could not tell which module a finding
# belonged to. They also failed the publication gate as unrecognised tracked paths, which is
# what refused the push on 25 Aug 2026. Instance data; the files stay on disk. See unit Z04.
.harness/exp-s02-audit-*/
.harness/orch-*/
.harness/s02-mut-*/
# Any future scratch tree that copies the package. The prefixes above are the
# two that were measured; this pattern is the one the ratchet names.
.harness/**/src/consilient/
